===Corinthians===
[[Sport Club Corinthians Paulista|Corinthians]] advanced to the final after a 1–0 win against [[Al Ahly SC|Al-Ahly]] on 12 December. [[Paolo Guerrero]] scored the winning goal with a header after thirty minutes.<ref>{{cite news |title=Corinthians book place in final with win over Al Ahly |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2012/dec/12/club-world-cup-corinthians-al-ahly |work=The Guardian |publisher=Guardian News and Media |agency=Reuters |date=12 December 2012 |access-date=12 December 2012 |archive-date=10 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160310072845/http://www.theguardian.com/football/2012/dec/12/club-world-cup-corinthians-al-ahly |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=Jim |last=Armstrong |title=Corinthians advance to final at Club World Cup |url=https://sports.yahoo.com/news/corinthians-advance-final-club-world-124511243--sow.html |work=Yahoo! Sports |publisher=Yahoo! |agency=Associated Press |date=12 December 2012 |access-date=12 December 2012 |archive-date=11 January 2013 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130111032216/http://sports.yahoo.com/news/corinthians-advance-final-club-world-124511243--sow.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>

===Chelsea===
Chelsea took on [[C.F. Monterrey|Monterrey]] on 13 December, winning 3–1 after goals from [[Juan Mata]], [[Fernando Torres]], and a [[Dárvin Chávez]] own goal. [[Aldo de Nigris]] scored a consolation goal for Monterrey in stoppage time.<ref>{{cite news |first=Gary |last=Rose |title=Monterrey 1–3 Chelsea |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/20658956 |work=BBC Sport |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |date=13 December 2012 |access-date=13 December 2012 |archive-date=12 January 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160112170102/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/20658956 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |first=James |last=Wrigley |title=Chelsea reach Club World Cup final after beating Monterrey |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/news-and-comment/chelsea-reach-club-world-cup-final-after-beating-monterrey-8412805.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220501/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/news-and-comment/chelsea-reach-club-world-cup-final-after-beating-monterrey-8412805.html |archive-date=1 May 2022 |url-access=subscription |work=The Independent|publisher=Independent Print |date=13 December 2012 |access-date=13 December 2012}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

==Pre-match==

===Venue===
The [[International Stadium Yokohama]] has been the venue for the FIFA Club World Cup since 2005. It was built and opened in 1998, and is the home ground of [[Yokohama F. Marinos]], who plays in the [[J. League Division 1|J. League]], the highest division of the [[Japanese association football league system|Japanese league system]]. The venue has been used five times in the previous FIFA Club World Championship and Club World Cup finals, in [[2005 FIFA Club World Championship|2005]], [[2006 FIFA Club World Cup|2006]], [[2007 FIFA Club World Cup|2007]] and [[2008 FIFA Club World Cup|2008]], as well as [[2011 FIFA Club World Cup|2011]].

===Match ball===
The official match ball for the final was the Adidas Cafusa, provided by German sports equipment company [[Adidas]]. It was used throughout the tournament and also at the [[2013 FIFA Confederations Cup]].<ref>{{cite news |title=adidas Cafusa launched at Brazil 2013 draw |url=https://www.fifa.com/confederationscup/news/newsid=1960502/index.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121204213534/http://www.fifa.com/confederationscup/news/newsid=1960502/index.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=4 December 2012 |work=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=15 December 2012 |access-date=15 December 2012}}</ref>

===Officials===
[[Cüneyt Çakır]], representing [[Turkish Football Federation|Turkey]] and UEFA, was selected as the referee of the final. He was first listed as an international referee in 2006,<ref>{{cite news |title=Referees – Cüneyt Çakır |url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/referees/referee=241952/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130320024205/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/referees/referee=241952/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=20 March 2013 |work=FIFA |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |date=14 December 2012 |access-date=14 December 2012}}</ref> and had earlier taken charge of his first FIFA Club World Cup match, the first quarter-final match between [[Ulsan Hyundai FC|Ulsan Hyundai]] and [[C.F. Monterrey|Monterrey]] on 9 December 2012. Çakır was assisted by Bahattin Duran and Tarık Ongun, while the fourth and fifth officials were [[Alireza Faghani]] and Hassan Kamranifar, representing the [[Football Federation Islamic Republic of Iran|Islamic Republic of Iran]] and one of the two [[Asian Football Confederation|AFC]] representatives in the competition, alongside [[Nawaf Shukralla]] of [[Bahrain Football Association|Bahrain]].

